From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:40:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] art: RegisterNatives bridge trampoline on every target build

GenerateNativeBridgeTrampoline only ran under ART_TARGET_ANDROID.
An ART_TARGET_LINUX runtime with a native bridge then registers the
raw guest pointer and enters guest code on the host thread pointer.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: a compile-time guard inside libart; launcher, loader and
 env cannot change it. The NativeBridge seam already has the callback
 (getTrampolineForFunctionPointer), the guard only keeps ART from
 calling it. Wrapping RegisterNatives in the bridge's guest JNIEnv
 instead is a second route that cannot see @CriticalNative (ArtMethod
 only) nor a host caller registering a guest pointer (b/393035780).
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 runtime/jni/jni_internal.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/jni/jni_internal.cc b/runtime/jni/jni_internal.cc
index 1dde2de74169940a9d6e6867e8bd2cb816fe5518..74142e8825e2ebc3f0cc6299d81aea055eb08ed4 100644
--- a/runtime/jni/jni_internal.cc
+++ b/runtime/jni/jni_internal.cc
@@ -2946,7 +2946,7 @@ class JNI {
 
   static const void* GenerateNativeBridgeTrampoline(const void* fn_ptr, ArtMethod* method)
       REQUIRES_SHARED(Locks::mutator_lock_) {
-#if defined(ART_TARGET_ANDROID)
+#if defined(ART_TARGET)
     uint32_t shorty_length;
     const char* shorty = method->GetShorty(&shorty_length);
     android::JNICallType jni_call_type = method->IsCriticalNative() ?
